<%#
  Lets a visitor change an analytics decision they already made.

  GDPR Art. 7(3) requires withdrawing consent to be as easy as giving it,
  and the banner only appears while no choice is stored. This clears the
  cookie and reloads, which brings the banner back.

  Rendered from every footer. The standalone pages (layout false) carry
  their own footers, so this is included in each rather than relying on
  layouts/_footer alone.
%>
<button type="button"
        onclick="document.cookie='analytics_consent=; path=/; max-age=0'; location.reload();"
        class="btn-plain bg-transparent border-0 shadow-none p-0 font-normal underline-offset-2 hover:underline hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer">
  <%= t("consent.settings") %>
</button>
